      "message": "This is a change in behavior, and will prevent a later abort when an API issue surfaces.\n\nThe M.O. to provide problem clarity and be able to triage is to abort as soon as you notice the problem and use the stack trace to resolve. I am not a \"frameworks guy\", but I expect they may prefer for example:\n\n// do not need the address, we have something more interesting, a stack trace!\nLOG_ALWAYS_FATAL(\"native surface not initialized, bufferage\u003d%d\", bufferage);\n\nand\n\nLOG_ALWAYS_FATAL(\"native surface missing\");\n\nrespectively. Please wait for a comment from someone that owns the framework before taking any action.",
